    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "305a6466_6ad36982",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T09:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change will let NetworkDiagnostics send DoT probes to all the plaintext DNS servers and all DoT servers whatever the mode is, or do you think the DoT probes should be based on the  mode? like no DoT probe in private DNS off mode?",
      "parentUuid": "54c40fdb_3488cc2c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 86,
        "endLine": 228,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42d38962_db370647",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-20T04:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see. I was thinking it would be good to avoid probing the servers if private DNS is disabled, because:\n1. That way we will not think that the probe failures indicate a problem:\n2. The diagnostics will complete more quickly when the servers do not reply to tcp/853 connections.\n\nThat said, disabled is likely rare (because the default is opportunistic) and we have the same problem in opportunistic anyway. This is good enough for now.",
      "parentUuid": "305a6466_6ad36982",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 86,
        "endLine": 228,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb97d2e7_66cda529",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 283,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T16:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What can be overwritten here? The UDP DNS measurements and the DoT measurements are in different hashtables, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab07f58a_ae03cf65",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 283,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T09:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If |target| is found in the both server lists, I think one probe is enough. For example: 8.8.8.8 can be a plaintext DNS server as well as a DoT server which is resolved by the name \"dns.google\". NetworkDiagnostics sends only one probe to it.\n\nNote that I don\u0027t follow the DnsResolver which doesn\u0027t verify the certificate in the opportunistic mode. All the DoT probes here requires valid certificates. If we want to support probes without certificate validation, it might be hard to implement it now and we can leave a TODO.",
      "parentUuid": "bb97d2e7_66cda529",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f920ee8_100fdbd5",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 283,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-20T04:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was confused by the comment until I tested this code and saw that it did both UDP and TLS measurements. (This is good.) I thought it would only do either UDP or TLS to a given IP address. (That would not have been great.)\n\nI think \"|target| can be a Do53 server as well as a DoT server\" is confusing because in the case of Do53 and DoT we do probe both UDP and DoT\". What we don\u0027t do is probe DoT twice on the same IP address. So maybe reword the comment to  \"This might overwrite an existing entry in mDnsTlsChecks, because |target| can be an IP address configured by the network as well as an IP address learned by resolving the strict mode DNS hostname\".\n\nAlso, can you say what happens if the measurement is overwritten? Maybe something like: \"if the entry is overwritten, the overwritten measurement thread executes as usual, but its results are not reported.\"\n\nAlways validating the cert here seems fine for now. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s difficult to to though (we can just set a null hostname verifier or something like that).\n\nOut of curiosity, what cert validation is used in opportunistic mode? Does the code validate that the server has a valid cert for the IP address? Or does it only check that the cert is unexpired? Or...?",
      "parentUuid": "ab07f58a_ae03cf65",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80e702c4_47cac361",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 283,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-20T08:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eOut of curiosity, what cert validation is used in opportunistic mode?\nAll of the DoT probes in this change use the system certificates for validation.\n\nIf I recall correctly, NetworkDiagnostics uses the default TrustManager instance (line 691), which loads the system certs from /system/etc/security/cacerts/, from Conscrypt for certificate validation. I didn\u0027t dig into the very detailed code though.",
      "parentUuid": "6f920ee8_100fdbd5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "64577ff5f9109f96b54d44438719734fd130eeb4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
