      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T16:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pre-existing, but I\u0027m not sure this is correct. I think the tag must remain set until all traffic is sent/received and the socket is closed. (I agree this is not a very intuitive API - I think would be much more intuitive to tag the socket, since that\u0027s what the underlying code actually does.)\n\nThat said - each measurement is on its own a thread right? If so, then why not do it just once, after the thread is started?\n\n    \n        @Override\n        public void run() {\n            if (ensureMeasurementNecessary()) return;\n\n            // No need to restore the tag, since this thread is only used for this measurement.\n            TrafficStats.setThreadStatsTag(TrafficStatsConstants.TAG_SYSTEM_PROBE);\n\n            ...",
